{"url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-06-23-agent/","category":"CompositeElement","chroma:document":"(2) Model selection: LLM distributes the tasks to expert models, where the request is framed as a multiple-choice question. LLM is presented with a list of models to choose from. Due to the limited context length, task type based filtration is needed.\n\nInstruction:\n\nGiven the user request and the call command, the AI assistant helps the user to select a suitable model from a list of models to process the user request. The AI assistant merely outputs the model id of the most appropriate model. The output must be in a strict JSON format: \"id\": \"id\", \"reason\": \"your detail reason for the choice\". We have a list of models for you to choose from {{ Candidate Models }}. Please select one model from the list.\n\n(3) Task execution: Expert models execute on the specific tasks and log results.\n\nInstruction:","element_id":"6271486d1888e0fd913dfc39756b1453","filetype":"text/html","link_texts":["AutoGPT","GPT-Engineer","BabyAGI","#","Prompt Engineering","#","#","Chain of thought","Wei et al. 2022","Yao et al. 2023","Liu et al. 2023","#","Yao et al. 2023","Shinn & Labash 2023","Liu et al. 2023","WebGPT comparisons","summarization from human feedback","human preference dataset","Laskin et al. 2023","UCB","Duan et al. 2017","#","conversations","#","Miller 1956","#","MIPS","LSH","ANNOY","HNSW","small world networks","FAISS","ScaNN","ann-benchmarks.com","#","Karpas et al. 2022","Parisi et al. 2022","Schick et al. 2023","â€œExternal APIsâ€ section","Plugins","function calling","Shen et al. 2023","Li et al. 2023","#","#","Bran et al. 2023","LangChain","ReAct","MRKLs","Boiko et al. (2023)","#","Park, et al. 2023","self-reflection","#","AutoGPT","GPT-Engineer","#","#","#","â€œChain of thought prompting elicits reasoning in large language models.â€","â€œTree of Thoughts: Dliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models.â€","â€œChain of Hindsight Aligns Language Models with Feedback â€œ","â€œLLM+P: Empowering Large Language Models with Optimal Planning Proficiencyâ€","â€œReAct: Synergizing reasoning and acting in language models.â€","â€œAnnouncing ScaNN: Efficient Vector Similarity Searchâ€","https://chat.openai.com/share/46ff149e-a4c7-4dd7-a800-fc4a642ea389","â€œReflexion: an autonomous agent with dynamic memory and self-reflectionâ€","â€œIn-context Reinforcement Learning with Algorithm Distillationâ€","â€œMRKL Systems A modular, neuro-symbolic architecture that combines large language models, external knowledge sources and discrete reasoning.â€","â€œWebgpt: Browser-assisted question-answering with human feedback.â€","â€œTALM: Tool Augmented Language Modelsâ€","â€œToolformer: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Use Tools.â€","Why is Vector Search so fast?","â€œAPI-Bank: A Benchmark for Tool-Augmented LLMsâ€","â€œHuggingGPT: Solving AI Tasks with ChatGPT and its Friends in HuggingFaceâ€","â€œChemCrow: Augmenting large-language models with chemistry tools.â€","â€œEmergent autonomous scientific research capabilities of large language models.â€","â€œGenerative Agents: Interactive Simulacra of Human Behavior.â€","https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","Nlp","Language-Model","Agent","Steerability","Prompting"],"emphasized_text_tags":["b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","b","b","i","b","i","b","i","b","b","i","b","i","b","i","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","i","i","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","b","b"],"link_urls":["https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","https://github.com/yoheinakajima/babyagi","#agent-system-overview","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/","#component-one-planning","#task-decomposition","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/#chain-of-thought-cot","https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903","https://arx