ling","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.17580","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.08244","#case-studies","#scientific-discovery-agent","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05376","https://github.com/hwchase17/langchain","#react","#mrkl","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05332","#generative-agents-simulation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442","#self-reflection","#proof-of-concept-examples","https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","#challenges","#citation","#references","https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903","https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.10601","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.02676","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.11477","https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.03629","https://ai.googleblog.com/2020/07/announcing-scann-efficient-vector.html","https://chat.openai.com/share/46ff149e-a4c7-4dd7-a800-fc4a642ea389","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.11366","https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.14215","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.00445","https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.09332","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.12255","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04761","https://weaviate.io/blog/why-is-vector-search-so-fast","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.08244","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.17580","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05376","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05332","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442","https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/nlp/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/language-model/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/agent/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/steerability/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/prompting/"],"chroma:document":"API-Bank (Li et al. 2023) is a benchmark for evaluating the performance of tool-augmented LLMs. It contains 53 commonly used API tools, a complete tool-augmented LLM workflow, and 264 annotated dialogues that involve 568 API calls. The selection of APIs is quite diverse, including search engines, calculator, calendar queries, smart home control, schedule management, health data management, account authentication workflow and more. Because there are a large number of APIs, LLM first has access to API search engine to find the right API to call and then uses the corresponding documentation to make a call.\n\nIn the API-Bank workflow, LLMs need to make a couple of decisions and at each step we can evaluate how accurate that decision is. Decisions include:\n\nWhether an API call is needed.\n\nIdentify the right API to call: if not good enough, LLMs need to iteratively modify the API inputs (e.g. deciding search keywords for Search Engine API).\n\nResponse based on the API results: the model can choose to refine and call again if results are not satisfied.","link_texts":["AutoGPT","GPT-Engineer","BabyAGI","#","Prompt Engineering","#","#","Chain of thought","Wei et al. 2022","Yao et al. 2023","Liu et al. 2023","#","Yao et al. 2023","Shinn & Labash 2023","Liu et al. 2023","WebGPT comparisons","summarization from human feedback","human preference dataset","Laskin et al. 2023","UCB","Duan et al. 2017","#","conversations","#","Miller 1956","#","MIPS","LSH","ANNOY","HNSW","small world networks","FAISS","ScaNN","ann-benchmarks.com","#","Karpas et al. 2022","Parisi et al. 2022","Schick et al. 2023","â€œExternal APIsâ€ section","Plugins","function calling","Shen et al. 2023","Li et al. 2023","#","#","Bran et al. 2023","LangChain","ReAct","MRKLs","Boiko et al. (2023)","#","Park, et al. 2023","self-reflection","#","AutoGPT","GPT-Engineer","#","#","#","â€œChain of thought prompting elicits reasoning in large language models.â€","â€œTree of Thoughts: Dliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models.â€","â€œChain of Hindsight Aligns Language Models with Feedback â€œ","â€œLLM+P: Empowering Large Language Models with Optimal Planning Proficiencyâ€","â€œReAct: Synergizing reasoning and acting in language models.â€","â€œAnnouncing ScaNN: Efficient Vector Similarity Searchâ€","https://chat.openai.com/share/46ff149e-a4c7-4dd7-a800-fc4a642ea389","â€œReflexion: an 