scientific research capabilities of large language models.â€","â€œGenerative Agents: Interactive Simulacra of Human Behavior.â€","https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","Nlp","Language-Model","Agent","Steerability","Prompting"],"emphasized_text_contents":["Planning","Memory","Tool use","Chain of thought","Tree of Thoughts","LLM+P","ReAct","Reflexion","decide to reset","Chain of Hindsight","Algorithm Distillation","algorithm","Sensory Memory","Short-Term Memory","Working Memory","Long-Term Memory","approximate nearest neighbors (ANN)â€‹","LSH","hashing","ANNOY","random projection trees","HNSW","FAISS","clustering","ScaNN","anisotropic vector quantization","MRKL","knowing when to and how to use the tools are crucial","TALM","Toolformer","HuggingGPT","(1) Task planning","(2) Model selection","(3) Task execution","(4) Response generation","API-Bank","call the API","retrieve the API","plan API beyond retrieve and call","ChemCrow","Generative Agents","Memory","observation","Retrieval","Reflection","higher-level summaries of past events","Planning & Reacting","Finite context length","Challenges in long-term planning and task decomposition","Reliability of natural language interface"],"category":"CompositeElement","languages":["eng"],"chroma:document":"The LLM is provided with a list of tool names, descriptions of their utility, and details about the expected input/output.\n\nIt is then instructed to answer a user-given prompt using the tools provided when necessary. The instruction suggests the model to follow the ReAct format - Thought, Action, Action Input, Observation.\n\nOne interesting observation is that while the LLM-based evaluation concluded that GPT-4 and ChemCrow perform nearly equivalently, human evaluations with experts oriented towards the completion and chemical correctness of the solutions showed that ChemCrow outperforms GPT-4 by a large margin. This indicates a potential problem with using LLM to evaluate its own performance on domains that requires deep expertise. The lack of expertise may cause LLMs not knowing its flaws and thus cannot well judge the correctness of task results.\n\nBoiko et al. (2023) also looked into LLM-empowered agents for scientific discovery, to handle autonomous design, planning, and performance of complex scientific experiments. This agent can use tools to browse the Internet, read documentation, execute code, call robotics experimentation APIs and leverage other LLMs.","element_id":"6271486d1888e0fd913dfc39756b1453","filetype":"text/html","url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-06-23-agent/"}␀␀␀␀␀␀¡‚IIðÔdàq4{␀␀␀°z␀␀␀à6ebHìár4{␀␀␀Ðz␀␀␀Ø•()±\~@r4{␀␀␀ðz␀␀␀6Ùl'2É>pr4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀ï?]7š]Þu r4{␀␀␀0z␀␀␀1ã5­Æl>˜Ðr4{␀␀␀Pz␀␀␀¤øîlÿäë␀s4{␀␀␀pz␀␀␀k-Å®íÂp°0s4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀zÖaOÏ~`s4{␀␀␀°z␀␀␀Áàn$Ûîµs4{␀␀␀Ðz␀␀␀ÉÜ¤»á“!XÀs4{␀␀␀ðz␀␀␀ŸLSFZGðs4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀æ&±—ÿ]p t4{␀␀␀0z␀␀␀¢¡1ì^Pt4{␀␀␀Pz␀␀␀™¨7ˆÜ“k€t4{␀␀␀pz␀␀␀ÜŸ•”éÞáÓ°t4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀½ë¿Èœ×àt4{␀␀␀°z␀␀␀yÙmNØU¯u4{␀␀␀Ðz␀␀␀®ê¿FNÂÅ@u4{␀␀␀ðz␀␀␀•^ÌåÀ¼­pu4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀¹"£Ž¼d u4{␀␀␀0z␀␀␀†C§–NZÕQÐu4{␀␀␀Pz␀␀␀{¥eÞÙ8^␀v4{␀␀␀pz␀␀␀Ô6ë‚J±¬0v4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀ûØ¬·¹`v4{␀␀␀°z␀␀␀W˜ÊßÄüÚÌv4{␀␀␀Ðz␀␀␀ÁˆYq¤WÀv4{␀␀␀ðz␀␀␀%òá_3\=ðv4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀4õj¸g‘R w4{␀␀␀0z␀␀␀€Yù»Ã¬š¯Pw4{␀␀␀Pz␀␀␀â£ŽÊÌÑËÿ€w4{␀␀␀pz␀␀␀#iÔœmn°w4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀×’ÅwSzºŸàw4{␀␀␀°z␀␀␀a1ævF›x4{␀␀␀Ðz␀␀␀w	±3x@x4{␀␀␀ðz␀␀␀hx—ý·r	px4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀|ró»Õô x4{␀␀␀0z␀␀␀á„ÊýŒ)ƒÐx4{␀␀␀Pz␀␀␀X:)B‰—~Ø␀y4{␀␀␀pz␀␀␀zò4Ä”¶—´0y4{␀␀␀z␀␀␀‹í␀+{Þ=5`y4{␀␀␀°z␀␀␀Ý­—Jãëy4{␀␀␀Ðz␀␀␀è»"‘ª³OÀy4{␀␀␀ðz␀␀␀'… és•ðy4{␀␀␀	z␀␀␀EEP†û«] z4{␀␀␀0	z␀␀␀¨þ¶<GÓ÷ÿPz4{␀␀␀P	z␀␀␀$êÁùiVµa€z4{␀␀␀p	z␀␀␀¦êß©¢Iæ°z4{␀␀␀	z␀␀␀mTqXÝ%àz4{␀␀␀°	z␀␀␀Ìo†o2{4{␀␀␀Ð	z␀␀␀Ñ]dë«ëþ@{4{␀␀␀ð	z␀␀␀Ë-ŸÂbû&¢p{4{␀␀␀
