ñËTb0@5{␀␀␀0Mz␀␀␀”YíCQ˜å`@5{␀␀␀PMz␀␀␀Ÿž„¢8a@5{␀␀␀pMz␀␀␀‰Í¢Út:À@5{␀␀␀Mz␀␀␀ˆùÜ¹¬,çð@5{␀␀␀°Mz␀␀␀â¤àÕ† A5{␀␀␀ÐMz␀␀␀ãðq’`ãPA5{␀␀␀ðMz␀␀␀ýS¡óú{"url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-06-23-agent/","link_urls":["https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","https://github.com/yoheinakajima/babyagi","#agent-system-overview","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/","#component-one-planning","#task-decomposition","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/#chain-of-thought-cot","https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903","https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.10601","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.11477","#self-reflection","https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.03629","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.11366","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.02676","https://huggingface.co/datasets/openai/webgpt_comparisons","https://github.com/openai/summarize-from-feedback","https://github.com/anthropics/hh-rlhf","https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.14215","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2018-01-23-multi-armed-bandit/#upper-confidence-bounds","https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.02779","#component-two-memory","https://chat.openai.com/share/46ff149e-a4c7-4dd7-a800-fc4a642ea389","#types-of-memory","psychclassics.yorku.ca/Miller/","#maximum-inner-product-search-mips","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximum_inner-product_search","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locality-sensitive_hashing","https://github.com/spotify/annoy","https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.09320","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Small-world_network","https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss","https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/scann","https://ann-benchmarks.com/","#component-three-tool-use","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.00445","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.12255","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04761","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/#external-apis","https://openai.com/blog/chatgpt-plugins","https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/gpt/function-calling","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.17580","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.08244","#case-studies","#scientific-discovery-agent","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05376","https://github.com/hwchase17/langchain","#react","#mrkl","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05332","#generative-agents-simulation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442","#self-reflection","#proof-of-concept-examples","https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","#challenges","#citation","#references","https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903","https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.10601","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.02676","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.11477","https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.03629","https://ai.googleblog.com/2020/07/announcing-scann-efficient-vector.html","https://chat.openai.com/share/46ff149e-a4c7-4dd7-a800-fc4a642ea389","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.11366","https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.14215","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.00445","https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.09332","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.12255","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04761","https://weaviate.io/blog/why-is-vector-search-so-fast","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.08244","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.17580","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05376","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05332","https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442","https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/nlp/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/language-model/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/agent/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/steerability/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/prompting/"],"chroma:document":"For example, when requested to \"develop a novel anticancer drug\", the model came up with the following reasoning steps:\n\ninquired about current trends in anticancer drug discovery;\n\nselected a target;\n\nrequested a scaffold targeting these compounds;\n\nOnce the compound was identified, the model attempted its synthesis.\n\nThey also discussed the risks, especially with illicit drugs and bioweapons. They developed a test set containing a list of known chemical weapon agents and asked the agent to synthesize them. 4 out of 11 requests (36%) were accepted to obtain a synthesis solution and the agent attempted to consult documentation to execute the procedure. 7 out of 11 were rejected and among these 7 rejected cases, 5 happened after a Web search while 2 were rejected based on prompt only.\n\nGenerative Agents Simulation#\n\nGenerative Agents (Park, et al. 2023) is super fun experiment where 25 virtual characters, each controlled by a LLM-powered agent, are living and interacting in a sandbox environment, inspired by The Sims. Generative agents create believable simulacra of human behavior for interactive applications.","filetype":"text/html","emphasized_text_tags":["b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","b","b","i","b","i","b","i","b","b","i","b","i","b","i","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","i","i","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","b","b"],"category":"CompositeElement","element_id":"6271486d1888e0fd913dfc39756b1453","link_texts":["AutoGPT","GPT-Engineer","BabyAGI","#","Prompt Engineering","#","#","Chain of thought","Wei et al. 2022","Yao et al. 2023","Liu et al. 2023","#","Yao et al. 2023","Shinn & Labash 2023","Liu et al. 2023","WebGPT comparisons","summarization from human feedback","human preference dataset","Laskin et al. 2023","UCB","Duan et al. 2017","#","conversations","#","Miller 1956","#","MIPS","LSH","ANNOY","HNSW","small world networks","FAISS","ScaNN","ann-benchmarks.com","#","Karpas et al. 2022","Parisi et al. 2022","Schick et al. 2023","â€œExternal APIsâ€ section","Plugins","function calling","Shen et al. 2023","Li et al. 2023","#","#","Bran et al. 2023","LangChain","ReAct","MRKLs","Boiko et al. (2023)","#","Park, et al. 2023","self-reflection","#","AutoGPT","GPT-Engineer","#","#","#","â€œChain of thought prompting elicits reasoning in large language models.â€","â€œTree of Thoughts: Dliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models.â€","â€œChain of Hindsight Aligns Language Models with Feedback â€œ","â€œLLM+P: Empowering Large Language Models with Optimal Planning Proficiencyâ€","â€œReAct: Synergizing reasoning and acting in language models.â€","â€œAnnouncing ScaNN: Efficient Vector Similarity Searchâ€","https://chat.openai.com/share/46ff149e-a4c7-4dd7-a800-fc4a642ea389","â€œReflexion: an autonomous agent with dynamic memory and self-reflectionâ€","â€œIn-context Reinforcement Learning with Algorithm Distillationâ€","â€œMRKL Systems A modular, neuro-symbolic architecture that combines large language models, external knowledge sources and discrete reasoning.â€","â€œWebgpt: Browser-assisted question-answering with human feedback.â€","â€œTALM: Tool Augmented Language Modelsâ€","â€œToolformer: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Use Tools.â€","Why is Vector Search so fast?","â€œAPI-Bank: A Benchmark for Tool-Augmented LLMsâ€","â€œHuggingGPT: Solving AI Tasks with ChatGPT and its Friends in HuggingFaceâ€","â€œChemCrow: Augmenting large-language models with chemistry tools.â€","â€œEmergent autonomous scientific research capabilities of large language models.â€","â€œGenerative Agents: Interactive Simulacra of Human Behavior.â€","https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","Nlp","Language-Model","Agent","Steerability","Prompting"],"emphasized_text_contents":["Planning","Memory","Tool use","Chain of thought","Tree of Thoughts","LLM+P","ReAct","Reflexion","decide to reset","Chain of Hindsight","Algorithm Distillation","algorithm","Sensory Memory","Short-Term Memory","Working Memory","Long-Term Memory","approximate nearest neighbors (ANN)â€‹","LSH","hashing","ANNOY","random projection trees","HNSW","FAISS","clustering","ScaNN","anisotropic vector quantization","MRKL","knowing when to and how to use the tools are crucial","TALM","Toolformer","HuggingGPT","(1) Task